# {{ ansible_managed }}
[Unit]
Description=Start a SMART short self-test on the homelab data disk

[Service]
Type=oneshot
# SHORT, not long, and that is measured rather than preferred. The long test
# was tried first on 2026-08-15: the drive announces 228 minutes for it, then
# returns "Completed: read failure" at LBA 730424728 within seconds — twice in a
# row, at the identical LBA — while that LBA and the 64 MiB around it read
# without error from the host, with every SMART counter at zero and nothing in
# dmesg. A WD50NDZW is a USB-native SMR drive whose bridge does not implement
# the extended self-test; the result is canned, not a finding. Building alerts
# on it would have meant a permanently red monitor.
#
# The short test does run properly here — it completed without error in the two
# minutes it announced. It exercises the electronics and a read sample, which is
# less than a surface scan but is real. Surface coverage comes from elsewhere:
# the nightly backup reads every file, and local-maintenance.sh runs a rotating
# `restic check --read-data-subset` over the repository.
ExecStart=/usr/sbin/smartctl -t short {{ data_disk_device | regex_replace('[0-9]+$', '') }}
